## Question Input

Renders the right answer control for one `SurveyQuestion`, picked by its `kind`: a single-line or multi-line text box, a single or multiple choice list, a 1–5 rating, or a yes/no pair. The value lives with the caller, who passes it in and receives every change.

```ts
import QuestionInput from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/survey/components/question-input';

<QuestionInput
  @question={{question}}
  @value={{this.answers.at(index)}}
  @onChange={{fn this.setAnswer index}}
  @invalid={{this.showRequired}}
/>
```

`@invalid` marks a required question the respondent tried to skip, so the caller decides when to show it. Multiple choice values are arrays; the other kinds are strings or numbers.

### Example

The linked Season Kickoff Fan Forum survey uses all six kinds, so its fill-in flow shows every control.

### Non-goals

No validation of its own beyond marking `@invalid`, and no persistence: the caller owns the answers and when they are saved.
